Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:46:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(shepherd):=20surface=20bot=20status=20sign?=
 =?UTF-8?q?als=20=E2=80=94=20StatusContext=20failures=20+=20bot=20status?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20comments=20(69e18ac6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GAP 1 — commit STATUSES (StatusContext), not just check-runs: isFailed now
classifies ERROR/STARTUP_FAILURE as failing, so a Vercel/Netlify-style commit
status (state=ERROR) is caught instead of looking pending. readState maps a
StatusContext's targetUrl into the detailsUrl slot alongside state→conclusion.

GAP 2 — plain bot STATUS COMMENTS (not review threads): new adapter
readIssueComments (paginated GraphQL) + a buildBotStatusBlockers scanner for
known status/deploy/quality bots (vercel, netlify, sonarqubecloud, codecov,
cloudflare-pages, cloudflare-workers-and-pages, render). It surfaces a
bot-status blocker only when the bot's LATEST comment signals failure (Quality
Gate failed, Deployment failed/error, dropped coverage, ❌...); a later success
supersedes an earlier failure. codecov stays automation for review THREADS but
its status COMMENT is scanned independently so it is never dropped as noise.

TDD: adapter StatusContext + readIssueComments tests, isFailed ERROR test,
scanner + computeBlockers + gatherPullSignal integration tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
